> **Mission:** Democratizing local manufacturing and resilient agritech through open-source hardware. Hera-Flux is a modular desktop fabrication lab designed to design, prototype, and produce real-world solutions like the **Prawn Guard** aquaculture monitoring system.

---

## 🌟 Overview
**Hera-Flux** is a comprehensive, modular home/hobby manufacturing fabrication lab built around a rigid 609.6 mm³ extruded aluminum rail frame (2020–80 series). 

Rather than a single machine, Hera-Flux is a compilation of open-source hardware projects organized into five prime functional frames, culminating in a **Desktop Electronics Lab (DEL)** capable of end-to-end PCB and IoT device production.

---

## 🏗️ The 5 Frames of Hera-Flux

| Frame | Function | Key Open-Source Inspirations |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **🖨️ Print** | FDM 3D Printing & Scanning | Venture XL, Voron 2.4 (ElecTray mod), OLSK 3D Scanner |
| **⚙️ CNC** | Precision Milling & Carving | Milo 2.0, OLSK-Small-CNC, CARVER X5 (5-Axis) |
| **✂️ Fab** | Laser Cutting & Plotting | OLSK Large Laser, OLSK Vinyl Cutter |
| **♻️ Form** | Plastic Recycling & Thermoforming | Precious Plastic Shredder, Open Shredder |
| **🔬 DEL (Desktop Electronics Lab)** | **PCB & IoT Production** | **LumenPnP (Pick & Place), Custom Stencil Printer/AOI** |

